  body: |
    # Territorial and transitional dates of coordination regulations

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source distinguishes Regulations 883/2004 and 987/2009 from the earlier regulations and records different start dates for EU Member States, Switzerland and Norway, Iceland and Liechtenstein, with transitional cases retained.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 071751 is a source-stated legal regime history: 1 May 2010, 1 April 2012 and 1 June 2012 have different territorial roles. Its word “current” is source wording, not a project claim of UK applicability in 2026. Post-transition instruments and individual scope remain unresolved.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 071751, PDF page 24](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a17044d050971fbebf3bb35/dmg-ch-07-part-02.pdf#page=24)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

